      <dc:creator>Weihao Ding Wu Chen Xiaolong Mi Qi Cheng Department of Land Surveying and Geospatial Science, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University, Hong Kong, ChinaWeihao Ding received his B.S. and M.S. degrees in Petroleum Engineering from Texas A&amp;M University in 2015 and 2017. He is currently pursuing the Ph.D. degree with the Department of Land Surveying and Geospatial Science, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. His current research interests include alternative approaches to ambiguity validation and positioning in difficult areas.Wu Chen received his Ph.D. degree from Newcastle University in 1992. He is currently a Professor with the Department of Land Surveying and Geospatial Science, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. His current research interests include the GNSS positioning quality evaluation, system integrity, various GNSS applications, seamless positioning and positioning technology for the future.Xiaolong Mi received dual Ph.D. degrees from the University of Chinese Academy of Sciences and Curtin University in 2022 and 2023, respectively. He is currently an Assistant Professor at the Department of Land Surveying and Geospatial Science, the Hong Kong Polytechnic University. His research interests include GNSS and LEO technologies for positioning, navigation, and timing (PNT) along with the application of artificial intelligence (AI) in earth and space sciences.Qi Cheng received the B.S. and M.S. degrees in Transportation Engineering from Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics in 2017 and 2021. He is currently pursuing the Ph.D. degree with the Department of Land Surveying and Geospatial Science, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. His research interest includes GNSS algorithms for intelligent transportation system (ITS) applications and urban environment.</dc:creator>
